# Inlining stress test: exercises the guard (correct fallback on a
# WRONG cached guess), num_registers widening + GC-root correctness
# under real allocation pressure from INSIDE an inlined callee, and a
# self-recursive function (must never be inlined into itself, but must
# still produce correct results via the ordinary fast-call path).

def helper_a(x) {
  return x * 2
}
def helper_b(x) {
  return x + 100
}

def caller(f, x) {
  return f(x)
}

# Warm `caller` up calling ONLY helper_a, so its call_target_cache
# learns helper_a as the guess at this call site.
var i = 0
while i < 300000 {
  caller(helper_a, i)
  i = i + 1
}

echo caller(helper_a, 10)
# The guard must catch this -- a different closure at the SAME call
# site the cache learned helper_a from. If the guard were missing or
# broken, this would wrongly run helper_a's inlined body (x*2 = 20)
# instead of falling back to a real call to helper_b (x+100 = 110).
echo caller(helper_b, 10)

# GC pressure from inside an inlined callee: `make_node` is a strong
# inlining candidate for `build`'s own hot loop. Each iteration
# allocates a real heap object THROUGH the (potentially inlined) call,
# forcing real GC passes to run while the inlined body's own widened
# register range is live -- exactly the scenario `num_registers`
# widening exists to keep sound (see `Chunk::num_registers`'s own
# docs): if GC's root-scan didn't cover the inlined callee's own
# registers, a live `Node` held only in an inlined-body-local register
# could be collected out from under still-executing code.
class Node {
  @new(v) {
    self.v = v
  }
}

def make_node(v) {
  return Node(v)
}

def build(n) {
  var total = 0
  var j = 0
  while j < n {
    var node = make_node(j)
    total = total + node.v
    j = j + 1
  }
  return total
}

echo build(500000)

# Self-recursion: fib must never inline a call to itself (see
# `jit::inlining`'s own docs), but must still produce correct results
# via the existing compiled-to-compiled fast-call path.
def fib(n) {
  if n < 2 {
    return n
  }
  return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)
}
echo fib(24)
